This testcase verifies that a dynamic load reads the importing callframe
after the module body ran.

The module body of chain0 runs the bodies of the modules it imports,
which pushes more callframes. When the callframe vector grows, realloc()
can move it, and a callframe pointer taken before the load then points
into freed memory.

This test depends on running under a memory checker.

-- Testcase --
let fn = loadstring('import { value } from "chain0";\nprint(value, "\\n");\n', {
	raw_mode: true,
	force_dynlink_list: [ 'chain0' ]
});

fn();
-- End --

-- File chain0.uc --
import { value as v } from "chain1";
export const value = v + 1;
-- End --

-- File chain1.uc --
import { value as v } from "chain2";
export const value = v + 1;
-- End --

-- File chain2.uc --
